        id: "emergence", term: "Emergence",
        definition: "The phenomenon in which properties, patterns, or forms arise in a system that could not have been predicted from the properties of the system's components taken individually. Emergence is creation without a creator: the new form is produced by the interactions of parts without any single part or external agent intending or designing it. The flock's murmuration, the ant colony's architecture, the market's price, the community's culture — all are emergent. In the context of creativity, emergence names what happens at the intersection of many creative acts: the surplus of collective making that no individual making intended. This is why genuine creativity is often more than the sum of its inputs.",
