        id: "commons-cg", term: "Commons / Commoning",
        definition: "Creation as collective, shared, and non-proprietary — the making of goods, knowledge, practices, and forms of life that belong to no one and therefore to everyone. Commoning, from Bollier and Helfrich, names the active process of creating and sustaining a commons: not a thing but an ongoing practice of negotiation, care, and collective stewardship. The commons is always being made; it is never simply given or preserved. In the context of this vocabulary, commoning is the specifically social form of generativity: the community that tends its commons is continuously creating the conditions for collective flourishing, and the commons that results is the emergent product of that continuous creative care.",
